# Integer division and MOD by zero.
#
# What the standard says: ed.3 6.6.1.5 (table 29 / 30) defines DIV and
# MOD; ed.2 annex E table E.1 lists "division by zero" as an error, with
# implementer-specific detection and reaction. Ed.3 states that an
# implementation-specific error reaction applies (the result is not
# defined). Note also that integer division of negative operands is
# defined as truncation toward zero (ed.2 2.5.1.5.2: "the result of DIV
# shall be truncated toward zero"), hence -7 / 2 = -3 and -7 MOD 2 = -1
# on cycle 1, which IS conformant and is kept here as context.
#
# What IronPLC 0.251.0 (5ea0610) does: the scan stops with the runtime
# trap "divide by zero" (VmFaulted); MOD by zero is not reached because the
# trap on the division ends the scan. Recorded 2026-10-31.
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: a b
outputs: q m
status: implementation-defined
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.2 annex E table E.1; ed.2 2.5.1.5.2 (DIV, MOD)
---
0 a=7 b=2 => q=3 m=1
1 a=-7 b=2 => q=-3 m=-1
2 a=7 b=0 => trap
